 this case, we have\n\n$$\np(x)={x}^{2},\\,q(x)={x}^{3},\\,n=-\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we multiply the differential equation by ${y}^{1/2},$ and we get\n\n$$\n{y}^{1/2}\\frac{dy}{dx}+{x}^{2}{y}^{3/2}={x}^{3}.\\,\\,(∗)\n$$\n\nThen, we make the substitution\n\n$$\nz={y}^{1-n}={y}^{3/2}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $z(x)$ using the chain rule, we get \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{3}{2}{y}^{1/2}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,⟹\\,{y}^{1/2}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{2}{3}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, equation $(∗)$ can be written as a linear equation in $z(x)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{2}{3}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+{x}^{2}\\,z={x}^{3}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write the above equation in standard form, which gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{3{x}^{2}}{2}\\,z=\\frac{3{x}^{3}}{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x)=\\frac{3{x}^{2}}{2}.$" 13194139535469 true] [17592186350771 1000 #edb/ref 17592186350772 13194139535469 true] [17592186350771 1000 #edb/ref 17592186350773 13194139535469 true] [17592186350771 1000 #edb/ref 17592186350774 13194139535469 true] [17592186350771 1000 #edb/ref 17592186350775 13194139535469 true] [17592186350771 1000 #edb/ref 17592186350776 13194139535469 true] [17592186350771 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535469 true] [17592186350771 1041 "selection" 13194139535469 true] [17592186350771 1104 #edb/ref 17592186350772 13194139535469 true] [17592186350771 1110 #uuid "64e28f49-279e-59d6-a4f2-1bc08558956e" 13194139535469 true] [17592186350772 1034 "\\frac{3{x}^{2}}{2}" 13194139535469 true] [17592186350772 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535469 true] [17592186350772 1111 #uuid "5a49fedd-ffc5-512b-a805-a87508b534c0" 13194139535469 true] [17592186350773 1034 "3{x}^{2}" 13194139535469 true] [17592186350773 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535469 true] [17592186350773 1111 #uuid "047f16b4-7eaa-5deb-b03e-e7f2bfd251e7" 13194139535469 true] [17592186350774 1034 "\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}" 131